# Koi: koi eat the food and each bite is a note (its ring: the middle low, the rim high); a white key
# drops food on its own ring; uneaten food may come back as memory; the shishi-odoshi knocks; Swim and Koi knobs
# (ZEN-1 boots into Sakura; PRESETS: the pond)
wait 800
spin PRESET 1
wait 1000
# the top black key tips the shishi-odoshi now; the others toss pebbles, each its own ring and bowl note (looked
# at 20 ms after: the pebble's note is at once, before a koi's bite can come between)
expect knob13 50
tapkey b10
wait 600
expect knocks 1
tapkey b0
wait 20
expect lastkey 6
tapkey b0
wait 20
expect lastkey 6
tapkey b9
wait 20
expect lastkey 15
expect pebbles 3
expect knob9 0
expect knob7 30
expect knob4 70
expect knob6 30
expect knob12 6
expect knob5 15
# Knock 0: it never knocks by itself, but the top black key still tips it
tap FX
tap FX
tap FX
spin K2 -50
expect knob13 0
wait 2000
tapkey b10
wait 2500
expect knocks 2
spin K2 50
expect knob13 50
wait 60000
expect koieaten >3
expect scnotes >3
expect nvoices <13
expect drones >0
shot pond.png
# the keyboard: a white key plays its note at once (sixteen notes from 6: w9 -> 15), and drops food on its ring
tapkey w9
wait 20
expect koinote 15
# food on keys' rings, and the koi come for it
tapkey w14
tapkey w6
tapkey w10
wait 40000
expect koieaten >8
# the shishi-odoshi tips within a couple of minutes; something has been remembered
wait 120000
# (two forced, and at Knock 50 one every 60-120 s by itself)
expect knocks >2
expect memories >0
# DRIFT: Swim (a list: Orbit -> School -> Orbit); MORE: Koi 5 -> 9 (a number: stops at 9)
wait 20000
shot school.png
spin K1 5
expect knob12 9
wait 5000
expect koieaten >10
# the night (the stone lantern lit, the koi pale): drawn and sent whole
dayat 0.7
wait 4000
shot night.png
expect stale 0
expect race 0
# every knob name and value fits its column
expect textfit 0
# back to the instrument: everything of the pond lets go
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 6000
expect mode 0
expect nvoices 0
# only what changed is sent to the screen; the screen as sent always matches the frame as drawn
expect stale 0
expect race 0
